  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "The molar solubility (in mol $\\mathrm{L}^{-1}$ ) of a sparingly soluble salt $M X_{4}$ is ${ }^{\\prime} S$. The corresponding solubility product is $K_{\\mathrm{sp}} . S$ in terms of $'K_{\\text {ip }}$' s given by the relation",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "FNvA9",
      "text": "$S=\\left(\\frac{K_{\\mathrm{s} \\rho}}{128}\\right)^{1 / 4}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "tmOp9",
      "text": "$S=\\left(\\frac{K_{s p}}{256}\\right)^{1 / 5}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hPFdL",
      "text": "$S=\\left(256 K_{s p}\\right)^{1 / 5}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3z6yS",
      "text": "$S=\\left(128 K_{\\mathrm{sp}}\\right)^{1 / 4}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\because$ For a compound $A_{x}B_{y}$\r\n$$\r\nK_{s p}=x^{x} \\cdot y^{y} \\cdot S^{x+y} . \\text { (where, } S=\\text { solubility })\r\n$$\r\nFor $M x_{4}$\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\nK_{\\mathrm{sp}}=1 \\times(4)^{4} \\cdot \\mathrm{S}^{1+4} \\\\\r\nK_{\\mathrm{sp}}=256 \\times \\mathrm{S}^{5}\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$\r\n$\\therefore S=\\left(\\frac{K_{s}}{256}\\right)^{1 / 5}$",
    "image": null
  },
